        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Culinary History - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nDEEP TIME ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────► PRESENT\n    │\n    ├── ~3.5 Mya: Oldowan tools, animal marrow access\n    │\n    ├── ~1 Mya: Hearth use (Wonderwerk Cave, South Africa)\n    │            Wrangham: cooked food → gut shortening → larger brain\n    │\n    ├── ~300 kya: Consistent fire use, Neanderthal cooking\n    │\n    ├── ~10,500 BP: Cereal domestication, Fertile Crescent\n    │\n    ├── ~6,000 BP: Mesopotamian beer civilization\n    │             Egyptian grain economy, pharaonic bread factories\n    │\n    ├── ~500 BCE: Greek symposium, Roman garum trade networks\n    │\n    ├── ~1000 CE: Medieval spice trade, Venice/Genoa intermediaries\n    │             Salting, smoking, pickling as preservation technology\n    │             Monastic brewing, distillation\n    │\n    ├── 1492–1600: Columbian Exchange — most transformative food event in history\n    │              Potato/tomato/chile/chocolate/maize → Old World\n    │              Wheat/cattle/sugar/pigs → New World\n    │\n    ├── 1700s–1800s: Haute cuisine codification (Carême → Escoffier)\n    │               Canning (Appert 1809), mechanical refrigeration (1876)\n    │               Industrialized slaughter, Birdseye freezing (1924)\n    │\n    ├── 1900s: Global food systems, processed food rise, Green Revolution\n    │\n    └── Present: Farm-to-table reaction, fermentation revival,\n                lab-grown meat, food system critique\n```"
    },
